'''Magistrate''' was a title used to describe a planetary or community head of state during the time of the [[Galactic Republic|Old Republic]], the [[Galactic Empire]], and the [[New Republic]]. Many Magistrates, such as [[Passel Argente]],<ref name="VE">''[[Star Wars: The Visual Encyclopedia]]''</ref> [[Greef Karga]],<ref name="Chapter 12">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 12: The Siege}}</ref> [[Morgan Elsbeth]], and Governor [[Wing]] wore ceremonial cloaks of office with ornamental clasps and a chain to denote their rank.<ref name="Chapter 13" />

Imperial wanted [[hologram]]s told readers in [[Aurebesh]] to inform their nearest magistrate if they had any information regarding rebel insurgents.<ref name="Steps" /> the term was also an authoritative legal title used by the [[Bastatha security forces]]. The [[Nikto]]s [[Tosta]] and [[Xun]] were both magistrates of [[Bastatha]], although they were in league with [[Rinnrivin Di]]'s [[Rinnrivin Di's cartel|cartel]].<ref name="Bloodline" /> The Galactic Empire too had their own magistrates, with one being bribed into pardoning a dealer on [[Tangenine]].<ref name="Twilight Company" /> [[Greef Karga]] was a magistrate before<ref name="Guide to Season One">[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian: Guide to Season One|''Star Wars: The Mandalorian'': Guide to Season One]]</ref> working for the [[Bounty Hunters' Guild]] on [[Nevarro]],<ref name="Chapter 8" /> later using the title as leader of the [[Nevarro City|city]] there and the surrounding area,<ref name="Chapter 12" /> later adopting the title of [[High Magistrate]].<ref name="Chapter 17">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 17: The Apostate}}</ref> The ruthless [[Morgan Elsbeth]] served as the magistrate of the city of [[Calodan]] on [[Corvus]], before being [[Liberation of Calodan|overthrown and replaced]] by Governor Wing.<ref name="Chapter 13" />

